    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# 4.05 — Sectional, Ricci and Scalar Curvature\n\n4.04 produced a tensor with $\\tfrac{1}{12}n^2(n^2-1)$ independent components — 20 in dimension 4. That is too much information to hold at once, so one takes **traces**, each throwing away structure in exchange for legibility.\n\n**Sectional curvature** loses nothing. For a 2-plane $\\sigma = \\mathrm{span}(X,Y) \\subset T_pM$,\n\n$$K(\\sigma) = \\frac{Rm(X,Y,Y,X)}{|X|^2|Y|^2 - \\langle X,Y\\rangle^2}.$$\n\nThis is the Gaussian curvature of the surface swept out by geodesics through $p$ tangent to $\\sigma$ — so it is Stage 3's $K$, recovered one plane at a time. Knowing $K(\\sigma)$ for *every* plane determines $Rm$ completely; it is a repackaging, not a reduction.\n\n**Ricci curvature** averages over planes. Contracting the first and last indices,\n\n$$\\mathrm{Ric}_{ij} = R^k_{\\;kij},$$\n\ngives a symmetric 2-tensor with $\\tfrac12 n(n+1)$ components — 10 in dimension 4. Geometrically $\\mathrm{Ric}(v,v)$ is $(n-1)$ times the average of $K(\\sigma)$ over planes containing $v$, and it controls how the **volume** of a small geodesic ball deviates from the Euclidean value. This is the curvature Einstein's field equations are written in.\n\n**Scalar curvature** traces once more:\n\n$$S = g^{ij}\\mathrm{Ric}_{ij},$$\n\na single function. For constant sectional curvature $K$,\n\n$$\\mathrm{Ric} = (n-1)K\\,g, \\qquad S = n(n-1)K.$$\n\nEach trace discards something. In dimension 2 nothing is lost — one component means $K$, $\\mathrm{Ric}$ and $S$ are equivalent. In dimension 3, $\\mathrm{Ric}$ has 6 components and so does $Rm$: still no loss. From **dimension 4** the counts diverge, $20 > 10$, and the difference is the **Weyl tensor** — the part of curvature invisible to $\\mathrm{Ric}$. That gap is why gravitational waves can travel through empty space.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"linearalgebra\")$\nratprint : false$\nts(e) := ratsimp(trigsimp(e))$\n\nchristoffel_hand(g, vars) := block([ginv, n_],\n  n_ : length(vars),  ginv : ratsimp(invert(g)),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( ginv[k][l]*( diff(g[j][l], vars[i])\n                        + diff(g[i][l], vars[j])\n                        - diff(g[i][j], vars[l]) ), l, 1, n_)/2 ),\n    j,1,n_), i,1,n_), k,1,n_) )$\n\n/* R^l_{ijk}, Lee's convention (see 4.04) */\nriem_hand(g, vars) := block([G, n_],\n  G : christoffel_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( diff(G[l][j][k], vars[i]) - diff(G[l][i][k], vars[j])\n        + sum( G[l][i][m]*G[m][j][k] - G[l][j][m]*G[m][i][k], m, 1, n_) ),\n    k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_), l,1,n_) )$\n\nriem_low_hand(g, vars) := block([Rr, n_],\n  Rr : riem_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( g[l][m]*Rr[m][i][j][k], m,1,n_) ),\n    l,1,n_), k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_) )$\n\n/* Ric_{ij} = R^k_{kij} : trace on the FIRST upper index and the first lower */\nricci_hand(g, vars) := block([Rr, n_],\n  Rr : riem_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  genmatrix( lambda([i,j], ts( sum( Rr[k][k][i][j], k, 1, n_) )), n_, n_) )$\n\nscalar_hand(g, vars) := block([Rc, ginv, n_],\n  Rc : ricci_hand(g, vars), ginv : ratsimp(invert(g)), n_ : length(vars),\n  ts( sum( sum( ginv[i][j]*Rc[i][j], j,1,n_), i,1,n_) ) )$\n\nassume(R0 > 0, u > 0, u < %pi, y > 0)$\n\n/* ---- sphere of radius R₀: constant K = 1/R₀², n = 2 ---- */\ng_sph : matrix([R0^2,0],[0,R0^2*sin(u)^2])$\nRc_s  : ricci_hand(g_sph, [u,v])$\nS_s   : scalar_hand(g_sph, [u,v])$\nK_s   : 1/R0^2$\nprint(\"SPHERE, radius R₀ (n = 2, K = 1/R₀²)\")$\nprint(\"   Ric      = \", Rc_s)$\nprint(\"   (n−1)K g = \", ratsimp((2-1)*K_s*g_sph))$\nprint(\"   difference = \", ratsimp(Rc_s - (2-1)*K_s*g_sph))$\nprint(\"   S = \", S_s, \"     n(n−1)K = \", ratsimp(2*1*K_s))$\n\n/* ---- hyperbolic half-plane: K = −1 ---- */\ng_hyp : matrix([1/y^2,0],[0,1/y^2])$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"HYPERBOLIC half-plane (n = 2, K = −1)\")$\nprint(\"   Ric = \", ricci_hand(g_hyp,[x,y]), \"   = (n−1)K g = \",\n      ratsimp(-1*g_hyp))$\nprint(\"   S   = \", scalar_hand(g_hyp,[x,y]), \"     n(n−1)K = \", -2)$\n\n/* ---- unit 3-sphere: the counts start to matter ---- */\ng_s3 : matrix([1,0,0],[0,sin(ch)^2,0],[0,0,sin(ch)^2*sin(te)^2])$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"UNIT 3-SPHERE (n = 3, K = 1)\")$\nprint(\"   Ric = \", ricci_hand(g_s3,[ch,te,ph]))$\nprint(\"   (n−1)K g = \", ratsimp(2*g_s3))$\nprint(\"   difference = \", ratsimp( ricci_hand(g_s3,[ch,te,ph]) - 2*g_s3 ))$\nprint(\"   S = \", scalar_hand(g_s3,[ch,te,ph]), \"     n(n−1)K = \", 6,\n      \"   (4.04 got 6 from ctensor ✓)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "SPHERE, radius R₀ (n = 2, K = 1/R₀²)\n   Ric      =  matrix([1,0],[0,sin(u)^2])\n   (n−1)K g =  matrix([1,0],[0,sin(u)^2])\n   difference =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   S =  2/R0^2      n(n−1)K =  2/R0^2\nHYPERBOLIC half-plane (n = 2, K = −1)\n   Ric =  matrix([-(1/y^2),0],[0,-(1/y^2)])    = (n−1)K g =\n         matrix([-(1/y^2),0],[0,-(1/y^2)])\n   S   =  -2      n(n−1)K =  -2\nUNIT 3-SPHERE (n = 3, K = 1)\n   Ric =  matrix([2,0,0],[0,2*sin(ch)^2,0],[0,0,2*sin(ch)^2*sin(te)^2])\n   (n−1)K g =  matrix([2,0,0],[0,2*sin(ch)^2,0],[0,0,2*sin(ch)^2*sin(te)^2])\n   difference =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n   S =  6      n(n−1)K =  6    (4.04 got 6 from ctensor ✓)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- Sectional curvature of an arbitrary 2-plane --- */\n/* NOTE: named secK, not sec — `sec` is Maxima's secant, and defining over it\n   fails with \"function name cannot be a built-in operator or special symbol\".\n   Same family of trap as `col`, `orbit`, `diag` elsewhere in this repo. */\nip(g, X, Y) := ts( sum( sum( g[i][j]*X[i]*Y[j], j,1,length(X)), i,1,length(X)) )$\n\nsecK(g, vars, X, Y) := block([Rm, n_, num, den],\n  Rm : riem_low_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  num : sum(sum(sum(sum(\n          Rm[i][j][k][l]*X[i]*Y[j]*Y[k]*X[l],\n        l,1,n_), k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_),\n  den : ip(g,X,X)*ip(g,Y,Y) - ip(g,X,Y)^2,\n  ts( num/den ) )$\n\n/* sanity: on the sphere every plane is the whole tangent space, K = 1/R₀² */\nprint(\"sphere, the only plane span(∂u,∂v):  K = \",\n      secK(g_sph, [u,v], [1,0], [0,1]))$\n\n/* --- A product: S² × ℝ, coords (u, v, w), g = diag(1, sin²u, 1) --- */\ng_prod : matrix([1,0,0],[0,sin(u)^2,0],[0,0,1])$\nvp : [u, v, w]$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"PRODUCT  S²(1) × ℝ,  g = \", g_prod)$\nprint(\"   K(∂u, ∂v) = \", secK(g_prod, vp, [1,0,0], [0,1,0]),\n      \"    the spherical factor\")$\nprint(\"   K(∂u, ∂w) = \", secK(g_prod, vp, [1,0,0], [0,0,1]),\n      \"    a plane containing the flat direction\")$\nprint(\"   K(∂v, ∂w) = \", secK(g_prod, vp, [0,1,0], [0,0,1]))$\n\n/* a one-parameter family of planes tilting from the sphere into ℝ */\nXt : [1, 0, 0]$\nYt : [0, cos(t)/sin(u), sin(t)]$          /* unit, orthogonal to Xt */\nKt : trigsimp( secK(g_prod, vp, Xt, Yt) )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   tilting the second vector by angle t out of the sphere:\")$\nprint(\"   K(t) = \", Kt)$\nprint(\"      t = 0     : \", ratsimp(subst(t=0, Kt)))$\nprint(\"      t = π/4   : \", ratsimp(subst(t=%pi/4, Kt)))$\nprint(\"      t = π/2   : \", ratsimp(subst(t=%pi/2, Kt)))$\nprint(\"   sectional curvature runs continuously from 1 down to 0.\")$\n\n/* --- Ricci as the average of sectional curvatures --- */\nRc_p : ricci_hand(g_prod, vp)$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   Ric = \", Rc_p, \"   — degenerate: the ℝ direction has Ric(∂w,∂w) = 0\")$\nprint(\"   S   = \", scalar_hand(g_prod, vp), \"   (= the sphere's S; ℝ adds nothing)\")$\navg : ratsimp( integrate(Kt, t, 0, 2*%pi) / (2*%pi) )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   average of K over the planes containing ∂u : \", avg)$\nprint(\"   (n−1)·average = \", ratsimp((3-1)*avg),\n      \"     Ric(∂u,∂u) = \", Rc_p[1][1], \"  ✓\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "sphere, the only plane span(∂u,∂v):  K =  1/R0^2\nPRODUCT  S²(1) × ℝ,  g =  matrix([1,0,0],[0,sin(u)^2,0],[0,0,1])\n   K(∂u, ∂v) =  1     the spherical factor\n   K(∂u, ∂w) =  0     a plane containing the flat direction\n   K(∂v, ∂w) =  0\n   tilting the second vector by angle t out of the sphere:\n   K(t) =  cos(t)^2\n      t = 0     :  1\n      t = π/4   :  1/2\n      t = π/2   :  0\n   sectional curvature runs continuously from 1 down to 0.\n   Ric =  matrix([1,0,0],[0,sin(u)^2,0],[0,0,0])\n            — degenerate: the ℝ direction has Ric(∂w,∂w) = 0\n   S   =  2    (= the sphere's S; ℝ adds nothing)\n   average of K over the planes containing ∂u :  1/2\n   (n−1)·average =  1      Ric(∂u,∂u) =  1   ✓"
          ]
        }
      ]
